---
description: How to implement a Jira story in this demo repo
alwaysApply: true
---

This repo is a live demo of Harness CI/CD to GKE. When asked to implement a Jira story:

1. Read the story (via the Jira/Atlassian MCP if connected, otherwise from the text pasted in chat).
2. Create a branch named `feature/<JIRA-KEY>-<short-slug>` from `main` (e.g. `feature/SHOP-1-holiday-promo`). Never commit to `main`. The Jira key in the branch name is how the Harness pipeline finds and updates the story.
3. Make the change in `src/config.js` unless the story clearly needs code elsewhere.
4. Keep `npm test` passing. If you add visible behaviour, add or update a test in `test/app.test.js`.
5. Commit with a message that starts with the Jira key, e.g. `SHOP-1: Launch holiday promo on the home page`.
6. Push the branch and open a pull request into `main` titled `<JIRA-KEY>: <summary>`. Do not merge it.

Do not change files under `deploy/` or `.harness/` for a feature story.
